## Context
Three facts the routing redesign treats as inputs are unverified:
1. `agents/*.md` carry `model: standard|strong`, which no adapter maps. What
   does Claude Code do with an unknown value: honour, ignore, inherit the
   session model? If ignored, the silent-inheritance risk already exists.
2. How do Pi and Codex choose a subagent's model? Pi addresses models by
   fully qualified provider id, so Pi may be a native cross-family door.
3. Can Codex launch Anthropic agents? (Used to decide that Codex needs no Sol
   recommendation.)

## Scope
One live probe per question with a positive control (a launch whose model is
known to be honoured) before trusting a null. Record the evidence in this
ticket's log. Do not edit repo files.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Q1 answered with a positive control, evidence in the log
- [ ] Q2 answered for Pi and Codex, evidence in the log
- [ ] Q3 answered, or marked unverified; if unverified at the end of A2 (1064), the Codex recommendation file says "no cross-family door; record `no report`"
